\fs96 \cf2 Get started with GPU programming\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 This tutorial introduces you to GPU programming with Mojo. You'll learn how to write a simple program that performs vector addition on a GPU, exploring fundamental concepts of GPU programming along the way.\
By the end of this tutorial, you will:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Understand basic GPU programming concepts like grids and thread blocks.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Learn how to move data between CPU and GPU memory.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Write and compile a simple GPU kernel function.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Execute parallel computations on the GPU.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Understand the asynchronous nature of GPU programming.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0
\cf2 We'll build everything step-by-step, starting with the basics and gradually adding more complexity. The concepts you learn here will serve as a foundation for more advanced GPU programming with Mojo. If you just want to see the finished code, you can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/modular/modular/tree/modular/v26.2/mojo/examples/gpu-intro"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 get it on GitHub}}.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
